  "worked_solution": "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2} & ={30}^{\u2218}+n\\cdot {180}^{\u2218}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the above equation for $x,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =2\\cdot {30}^{\u2218}+2\\cdot n\\cdot {180}^{\u2218} \\\\ x & ={60}^{\u2218}+n\\cdot {360}^{\u2218}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $a={60}^{\u2218}.$",
